==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|careless|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɛɹləsli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɛələsli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carelessly.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Giving the appearance of [[carelessness]]; [[relaxedly]].
#: {{ux|en|The papers were '''carelessly''' strewn on the table.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=1920-03|author=Alice Ballantine Kirjassoff|title=FORMOSA THE BEAUTIFUL|journal=National Geographic Magazine|url=https://archive.org/details/nationalgeograp371920nati/page/264|page=264|text=Let us try to imagine the qualms of some Fifth Avenue florist if he could but see so many potential boutonnières, at a dollar apiece, so '''carelessly''' heaped up in baskets, lining the dingy pavement.}}
# Done without care or attention; [[inattentively]].
#: {{ux|en|Distracted by the salesperson, he '''carelessly''' read the contract.}}

